  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="99402f9a-a336-4a0e-a2d3-09edacc50f47"><problem><para>
      <para>Find the value of each specified term of the arithmetic sequences below. Hint: Enter your answers as an integer only. Do not include commas or periods.</para>
        <para>Find the \(21^{st}\) term of a sequence where the first term is \(3\) and the common difference is \(8\).
          </para>
        </para></problem><solution><para>163</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(163\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="a213731c-aa53-490d-a01a-b1b95c11851b"><problem><para>
      <para>A sequence consists of the following terms: 1280, 320, 80, … What is the explicit formula for this sequence? </para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(a_n = 1280 - 960(n-1)\)</para><para>\(a_n = 1280 (4)^{n-1}\)</para><para>\(a_n = 1280 (\frac 14)^{n-1}\)</para><para>\(a_n = 1280 \div 4(n-1)\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(a_n = 1280 (\frac 14)^{n-1}\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(a_n = 1280 (\frac 14)^{n-1}\) . </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
